      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Yahh ‘Ezrati Min Shəmayya” was written by Ḥayyim Shaul Aboud, a 20th century sage who taught and wrote piyyutim. Many of R’ Aboud’s compositions were meant to be sung to popular Arabic melodies of his time. Therefore, this piyyut follows the verse-chorus pattern one would expect to see in popular music, and is often sung antiphonally (call-and-response.)</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_30704_notes"/>
